---
/*
  /lab/custom/ — iteration 2, surface-choice page built to FIX the
  "reader saw just two fonts" problem.

  Earlier iteration pages set five body faces that were too alike to perceive
  as different (three lookalike transitional serifs + two plain sans). This page
  uses six body faces with strong individual character — a calligraphic humanist
  serif, a grotesque sans, a slab serif, a geometric sans, a high-contrast serif,
  and a mono — each visibly distinct from the others and from everything used for
  body before. None of Newsreader / Spectral / Source Serif 4 / Cuprum / Hanken
  Grotesk is used for body anywhere on this page.

  Body faces, per block:
    B1 body        → Lora            (calligraphic humanist serif)
    B2 list        → Work Sans       (grotesque sans)
    B3 list        → Bitter          (slab serif)
    B4 stat text   → Manrope         (geometric sans) · figures → IBM Plex Mono
    B5 body        → Frank Ruhl Libre (high-contrast serif) · doc → IBM Plex Mono
    B6 body        → Lora            (calligraphic humanist serif)
    B7 body        → Bitter          (slab serif)

  Headings alternate the display roster, no consecutive repeat:
    B1 Fraunces · B2 Ubuntu Condensed · B3 Space Mono · B4 Chakra Petch ·
    B5 Oxanium · B6 Cuprum · B7 Nova Square.

  §4 catalog used: solid-inside/gradient-outside (B1, B4), double-outline (B2),
  accent-tint color band (B3), carved bare frame (B5), sidenote card (B6),
  inverse near-black block (B7). Card vs full-bleed band alternated. Gradients
  live on the GROUND outside any lined/carded block; interiors stay solid.

  Own shell — no BaseLayout. Static. Content verbatim (§5). B3 CTA → /varpage/teardown/.
*/
import LabMenu from '../../components/LabMenu.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>/lab/custom — distinct body faces</title>
  <meta
    name="description"
    content="Iteration 2 surface-choice page: six visibly distinct body faces (Lora, Work Sans, Bitter, Manrope, IBM Plex Mono, Frank Ruhl Libre), alternated grounds, one strong accent per block, §4 block catalog."
  />

  <!-- Fonts via Google Fonts. Every family on the page — bodies AND headings —
       is in this one link (bodies: Lora, Work Sans, Bitter, Manrope, IBM Plex
       Mono, Frank Ruhl Libre; headings: Fraunces, Ubuntu Condensed, Space Mono,
       Chakra Petch, Oxanium, Cuprum, Nova Square). LabMenu uses Space Mono. -->
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bitter:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&family=Chakra+Petch:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Cuprum:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;500;700&family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,400;0,9..144,600;1,9..144,400&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&family=Lora:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;1,400&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Nova+Square&family=Oxanium:wght@400;600;700&family=Space+Mono:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=Ubuntu+Condensed&family=Work+Sans:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;1,400&display=swap"
    rel="stylesheet"
  />

  <style is:global>
    :root {
      /* Base whites — clean near-white base, alternated warm/cool grounds */
      --cool: #FCFCFB;        /* clean cool near-white — base surface */
      --warm: #FAF9F5;        /* warm off-white */
      --warm-lift: #FAF5EC;   /* warmer near-white — soft end of warm gradient */
      --blue-tint: #EDF1FD;   /* soft blue tint — cool gradient end */
      --clay-wash: #F7EBE4;   /* soft clay wash — accent-tint band */
      --clay-wash-deep: #F0DACE;

      /* Inks */
      --ink: #1B1C1F;
      --ink-soft: rgba(27, 28, 31, 0.66);
      --ink-mute: rgba(27, 28, 31, 0.54);

      /* Inverse ground (near-black block) */
      --dark: #17181C;
      --dark-deep: #101115;
      --paper: #F4F3EE;
      --paper-soft: rgba(244, 243, 238, 0.68);

      /* Accents — real hues, one strong per block */
      --orange: #D2691E;      --orange-deep: #B4571A;
      --blue: #2F5FE0;        --blue-deep: #2249B8;
      --clay: #CC785C;        --clay-deep: #B15F44;
      --teal: #0E7C66;        --teal-deep: #0A6352;

      /* Rules */
      --rule: #E5E3DC;
      --rule-cool: #E2E5E8;
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--cool);
      color: var(--ink);
      /* No single default body face — every block sets its own distinct font. */
      font-size: 20px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
    }

    .page { display: block; }

    /* One block = one editing treatment. Wide, airy grounds. */
    .blk { padding: 5.5rem 1.5rem; }

    /* Gradient grounds — outside any lined/carded block; interiors stay solid. */
    .g-warm  { background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--cool) 0%, var(--warm-lift) 100%); }
    .g-flat-warm { background: var(--warm); }
    .g-blue  { background: linear-gradient(175deg, var(--cool) 0%, var(--blue-tint) 100%); }
    .g-cool  { background: var(--cool); }

    /* Wide measures — no skinny columns. */
    .col   { max-width: 76ch; margin-inline: auto; }
    .col-w { max-width: 82ch; margin-inline: auto; }
    .wrap-w{ max-width: 84ch; margin-inline: auto; }

    /* Captions: italic, muted, ≤16, set in the block's own BODY font. */
    .cap { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-mute); margin-top: 1.9rem; }
    .cap em { font-style: italic; }
    .note { font-size: 16px; color: var(--ink-soft); }

    a { color: var(--orange); text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
    a:hover { color: var(--orange-deep); }

    /* ---------- B1 — premise (prose) — Stripe Press ----------
       Solid-inside / gradient-outside: solid white carved card on a
       white↔soft-warm gradient ground. Fraunces head + LORA body. */
    .b1-card {
      background: #FFFFFF;
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rule);
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 2.6rem 2.4rem;
    }
    .b1-eyebrow {
      font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
      font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--orange); margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }
    .b1-head {
      font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
      font-weight: 600; font-size: 38px; line-height: 1.15;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
    }
    .b1-body { font-family: 'Lora', Georgia, serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }

    /* ---------- B2 — palette + surface (rhythm list) — Linear ----------
       DOUBLE-OUTLINE: two thin borders 3px apart, solid white inside. Heading
       takes the blue accent. Ubuntu Condensed head + WORK SANS items. */
    .b2-card {
      background: #FFFFFF;
      border: 1px solid var(--blue);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px #FFFFFF, 0 0 0 4px var(--blue);
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 1.4rem 2rem;
    }
    .b2-eyebrow {
      font-family: 'Work Sans', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px;
      letter-spacing: 0.4px; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--blue); margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    }
    .b2-head {
      font-family: 'Ubuntu Condensed', sans-serif;
      font-size: 44px; line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.022em;
      color: var(--blue-deep); margin: 0 0 1.9rem;
    }
    .b2-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
    .b2-list li {
      font-family: 'Work Sans', sans-serif;
      font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.55;
      padding-block: 1.05rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-cool);
    }
    .b2-list li:first-child { border-top: none; }
    .b2-list li b { font-weight: 600; color: var(--blue-deep); }

    /* ---------- B3 — long-text handling (list) + CTA — 37signals ----------
       ACCENT-TINT COLOR BLOCK, full-bleed BAND: soft-clay wash with contrasting
       dark text (a band, not a lined card, so a soft gradient is allowed here).
       Space Mono head + BITTER slab reading. */
    .band-clay {
      background: linear-gradient(160deg, var(--clay-wash) 0%, var(--clay-wash-deep) 100%);
      color: #2A1810;
    }
    .b3-head {
      font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
      font-weight: 700; font-size: 32px; line-height: 1.18;
      color: var(--clay-deep); margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    }
    .b3-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 2.2rem; font-family: 'Bitter', serif; }
    .b3-list li { font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0 0 1.2rem; }
    .b3-list b { font-weight: 600; }
    .b3-cta { margin-top: 0.4rem; }
    .btn {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 19px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.01em;
      background: var(--ink); color: var(--clay-wash);
      padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none;
    }
    .btn:hover { background: #000; color: var(--clay-wash); }

    /* ---------- B4 — block rhythm (stat-dense) — Stripe ----------
       Solid-inside / gradient-outside: solid white carved stat cards on a
       white↔soft-blue gradient ground. Chakra Petch head + MANROPE text,
       IBM PLEX MONO figures. Teal accent. */
    .b4-eyebrow {
      font-family: 'Chakra Petch', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; letter-spacing: 0.02em;
      text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--teal-deep); margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
    }
    .b4-grid { display: grid; gap: 1.15rem; }
    .b4-stat {
      background: #FFFFFF;
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rule-cool);
      border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem 1.7rem;
    }
    .b4-fig {
      font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
      font-size: 30px; line-height: 1.15; font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--teal); margin: 0 0 0.55rem;
    }
    .b4-src { font-family: 'Manrope', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; }

    /* ---------- B5 — bare imagery (bare frame / doc-excerpt) ----------
       Carved single frame on cool near-white; no images — the monospace
       document IS the image. Oxanium head + FRANK RUHL LIBRE body +
       IBM PLEX MONO doc-excerpt. Orange accent. */
    .b5-head {
      font-family: 'Oxanium', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-weight: 600; font-size: 32px; line-height: 1.15;
      color: var(--orange-deep); margin: 0 0 1.3rem;
    }
    .b5-body { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', Georgia, serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 1.9rem; }
    .bare { margin: 0; }
    .doc-excerpt {
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rule);
      border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.6rem;
      background: #FFFFFF;
      font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
      font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ink-soft);
      white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-x: auto;
    }
    .doc-excerpt .anno { color: var(--orange); }
    figcaption { margin-top: 1rem; }

    /* ---------- B6 — the 2026 warning (sidenote) — Works in Progress ----------
       Flat warm off-white ground; teal accent. Cuprum head + LORA body,
       teal margin note. */
    .b6-head {
      font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 700; font-size: 40px; line-height: 1.12;
      color: var(--teal-deep); margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
    }
    .b6-wrap { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 70ch) 16rem; gap: 2.6rem; align-items: start; }
    .b6-body { font-family: 'Lora', Georgia, serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
    .b6-side {
      font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif;
      font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--teal);
      padding-top: 0.35rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--teal); padding-left: 1rem;
    }
    @media (max-width: 860px) { .b6-wrap { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

    /* ---------- B7 — harvest close (statement) ----------
       INVERSE BLOCK: near-black full-bleed band dropped into the light page,
       whisper focal gradient toward darker. Orange headline. Nova Square head +
       BITTER slab body, paper text. */
    .band-dark {
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--dark) 0%, var(--dark-deep) 100%);
      color: var(--paper);
    }
    .b7-head {
      font-family: 'Nova Square', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-size: 44px; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      color: var(--orange); margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
    }
    .b7-body { font-family: 'Bitter', serif; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--paper); margin: 0; }
    .b7-body + .b7-body { margin-top: 1.1rem; }
    .band-dark .cap { color: var(--paper-soft); }

    /* Per-block caption fonts — each caption set in its block's own BODY font. */
    .b1-cap { font-family: 'Lora', Georgia, serif; }
    .b2-cap { font-family: 'Work Sans', sans-serif; }
    .b3-cap { font-family: 'Bitter', serif; color: rgba(42, 24, 16, 0.62); }
    .b4-cap { font-family: 'Manrope', sans-serif; }
    .b5-cap { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', Georgia, serif; }
    .b6-cap { font-family: 'Lora', Georgia, serif; }
    .b7-cap { font-family: 'Bitter', serif; }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <LabMenu active="custom" />
  <main class="page">

    <!-- ============ B1 — premise (prose) ============ -->
    <!-- template: prose · treatment: Stripe Press (solid card, gradient-outside ground) -->
    <section class="blk g-warm">
      <div class="col">
        <div class="b1-card">
          <p class="b1-eyebrow">Premise</p>
          <h1 class="b1-head">A live site is a better template source than a marketplace.</h1>
          <p class="b1-body">Your premise holds. A live site is a better template source than a template marketplace, because you can read the decisions rather than inherit someone's content model. And the reskin is only about six variables: neutral ramp, one accent, radius scale, spacing scale, text measure, border weight. Fix those six and any layout you admire becomes yours.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="cap b1-cap"><em>Feel: warm, calligraphic, book-like. Lora 21/1.6 body + Fraunces 38 head · 76ch · solid white carved card on a white↔soft-warm gradient ground · orange accent — similar to Stripe Press.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ B2 — palette + surface (rhythm list) ============ -->
    <!-- template: rhythm-list · treatment: Linear (double-outline card) -->
    <section class="blk g-flat-warm">
      <div class="col-w">
        <p class="b2-eyebrow">Palette + surface</p>
        <h2 class="b2-head">The white-main systems worth copying wholesale</h2>
        <div class="b2-card">
          <ul class="b2-list">
            <li><b>Mercury</b> — the reference for premium-restrained off-white. Near-invisible borders, almost no shadow, one accent used sparingly. Serious without being cold, which is your construction-buyer problem exactly.</li>
            <li><b>Anthropic</b> — warm ivory ground, serif headings, very low saturation. Closest live example of your §1 brief: calm enough to read as a default rather than a pitch.</li>
            <li><b>Attio</b> — white, precise, tight grid. Shows how far a single accent goes when everything else is neutral.</li>
            <li><b>Notion</b> — the smoothed-edges reference. Radius scale, soft card fills, warm white. Study it for where rounding stops; over-rounding is what makes a premium site read as a toy.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="cap b2-cap"><em>Feel: crisp, plain-spoken, structural. Work Sans 20/1.55 grotesque items + Ubuntu Condensed 44 blue head · 82ch · double-outline card (2×1px, 3px apart), solid white inside on flat warm off-white · blue accent — similar to Linear.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ B3 — long-text handling (list) + CTA ============ -->
    <!-- template: prose-list + plain-cta · treatment: 37signals/Basecamp (accent-tint color band) -->
    <section class="blk band-clay">
      <div class="col-w">
        <h2 class="b3-head">Long-text handling</h2>
        <ul class="b3-list">
          <li><b>Stripe Press</b> — book typography on the web. Measure control, no chrome, headings that hold their own without decoration.</li>
          <li><b>Works in Progress</b> — sidenotes, footnotes, sustained reading. Relevant to your Notion-docs layer and the sample teardowns.</li>
          <li><b>37signals / Basecamp</b> — plain speech, opinionated blocks, one CTA, active refusal of decoration. The nearest ethos match to your §6 and §9.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="b3-cta">
          <a class="btn" href="/varpage/teardown/">Request a free teardown &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <p class="cap b3-cap"><em>Feel: sturdy, slab-set, one clear ask. Bitter 21/1.55 slab reading + Space Mono 32 head, one ink CTA · 82ch · full-bleed soft-clay wash band (contrasting dark text), no lined card · clay accent — similar to 37signals / Basecamp.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ B4 — block rhythm and sequencing (stat-dense) ============ -->
    <!-- template: stat-dense · treatment: Stripe (solid cards, gradient-outside ground) -->
    <section class="blk g-blue">
      <div class="col-w">
        <p class="b4-eyebrow">Block rhythm and sequencing — big SaaS</p>
        <div class="b4-grid">
          <div class="b4-stat">
            <div class="b4-fig">Linear</div>
            <p class="b4-src">take the spacing rhythm and the restraint, invert the palette. The lesson is vertical rhythm, and whitespace used structurally.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="b4-stat">
            <div class="b4-fig">Stripe</div>
            <p class="b4-src">how to sequence dense information so density stops feeling heavy. Useful for your §5, where you have a statistic plus a source plus a caveat in one block.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="cap b4-cap"><em>Feel: geometric, calm-dense, sequenced. Manrope 20/1.55 stat text + IBM Plex Mono 30 figures, Chakra Petch head · 82ch · solid white carved cards on a white↔soft-blue gradient ground · teal accent — similar to Stripe.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ B5 — bare imagery (bare frame / doc-excerpt) ============ -->
    <!-- template: bare-frame · treatment: Stripe (carved frame, no image) -->
    <section class="blk g-cool">
      <div class="col-w">
        <h2 class="b5-head">Bare imagery</h2>
        <p class="b5-body">Mercury, Ramp, and Arc all show images without device frames, drop shadows, or perspective tilt. That is the current premium signal, and it happens to be the only image treatment that fits you.</p>
        <figure class="bare">
          <div class="doc-excerpt"><span class="anno"># teardown — annotation layer</span>
&gt; hero      no device frame · no shadow · no tilt
&gt; measure   82ch
&gt; radius    8px
&gt; border    1px inner (carved)
<span class="anno">&gt; note      the artifact IS the image</span></div>
          <figcaption class="note">Bare frame stands in for the image: a monospace document excerpt, no chrome.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="cap b5-cap"><em>Feel: high-contrast, document-like, no chrome. Frank Ruhl Libre 21/1.6 body + IBM Plex Mono 16 doc-excerpt, Oxanium head · 82ch · solid white carved frame on cool near-white · orange accent — similar to Stripe.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ B6 — the 2026 warning (sidenote) ============ -->
    <!-- template: sidenote · treatment: Works in Progress (flat ground, margin note) -->
    <section class="blk g-flat-warm">
      <div class="wrap-w">
        <h2 class="b6-head">One warning about the 2026 consensus</h2>
        <div class="b6-wrap">
          <div>
            <p class="b6-body">Every roundup this year says the same three things: put the product in motion at the top, add micro-interactions, consider dark mode. Two of those are wrong for you. You have no product UI to demo, and dark mode fights the calm-default frame you decided to install. Your equivalent of the interactive product moment is a real teardown excerpt rendered as a document — styled like a page from the artifact the client would receive, monospace annotations and all. That is your hero image and your §7 proof in one object.</p>
          </div>
          <aside class="b6-side">That is your hero image and your §7 proof in one object.</aside>
        </div>
        <p class="cap b6-cap"><em>Feel: warm, calligraphic, annotated. Lora 21/1.6 serif body + Cuprum 40 teal head · 70ch main + 16rem teal margin note · flat warm off-white, no lined card · teal accent — similar to Works in Progress.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ B7 — harvest close (statement) ============ -->
    <!-- template: statement · treatment: Stripe Press (inverse near-black band, focal grad) -->
    <section class="blk band-dark">
      <div class="col">
        <h2 class="b7-head">Five numbers and two fonts.</h2>
        <p class="b7-body">Open each of these, then write down only: the radius value, the body measure in characters, the border color and weight, the ratio between section padding and paragraph spacing, the type pairing. Five numbers and two fonts.</p>
        <p class="b7-body">That set, applied to any block library, gets you closer to a coherent site than any theme purchase will.</p>
        <p class="cap b7-cap"><em>Feel: sturdy, slab-set, high-contrast close. Bitter 21/1.6 slab body + Nova Square 44 orange head · 76ch · inverse near-black full-bleed band with a whisper focal gradient (toward darker), no lined card · orange accent — similar to Stripe Press.</em></p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</body>
</html>
